<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 4.294 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT	 TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	150 million    359 days   23.05 pct</p>
<p>	150 million    177 days   21.90 pct</p>
<p>	150 million     86 days   20.80 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    1.000 bln     38 days   20.28 pct</p>
<p>	700 million     24 days   19.84 pct</p>
<p>	750 million     15 days   19.58 pct</p>
<p>    1.000 bln	9 days   19.56 pct</p>
<p>	394 million	1 day    19.69 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
